Static packaged agent files are compatibility artifacts only. Runtime delegation uses Antigravity `define_subagent` once per required rp1-derived type in the active session, then `invoke_subagent` with the cached `TypeName`. Nested delegation is disabled unless a definition explicitly marks `nestedDelegation.enabled` and `defineSubagent.enable_subagent_tools` as true.

## Runtime Roots And Boundaries

Tracked workflows bootstrap with `CURRENT_HOST=antigravity` and `--harness antigravity`. The bootstrap response owns all runtime paths: source-code operations use `codeRoot`, knowledge reads use `kbRoot`, and durable rp1 artifacts use `workRoot`. Worktree runs must preserve the canonical `projectRoot`/`workRoot` plus active-worktree `codeRoot` split.

Treat permissions, trust prompts, sandbox limits, headless execution, MCP access, external workspaces, isolated worktrees, and nested delegation as support-matrix-controlled modes. If a mode is unsupported or lacks Antigravity validation evidence, report an Antigravity support exception with the next manual action instead of continuing silently.

## Support Matrix

The generated `support-matrix.json` file is the product support boundary for Antigravity workflows. Unsupported entries are product-owned exceptions with a rationale and user action, not missing generated assets.
